.TH SDL_LoadFile_IO 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_LoadFile_IO \- Load all the data from an SDL data stream.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_iostream.h>
.PP
.BI "void * SDL_LoadFile_IO(SDL_IOStream *src, size_t *datasize, bool closeio);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The data is allocated with a zero byte at the end (null terminated) for convenience\[char46] This extra byte is not included in the value reported via
.BR datasize \[char46]
.PP
The data should be freed with
.BR SDL_free ()\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I src
the
.BR SDL_IOStream
to read all available data from\[char46]
.TP
.I datasize
a pointer filled in with the number of bytes read, may be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I closeio
if true, calls
.BR SDL_CloseIO ()
on
.BR src
before returning, even in the case of an error\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the data or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
Do not use the same
.BR SDL_IOStream
from two threads at once\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_LoadFile (3),
.BR SDL_SaveFile_IO (3)
